description:
## Problem

`packages/authoring-ui/src/jsfl/runtime.ts` `setFrameProperty` (around line 959) is missing two commonly-used Flash 8 JSFL property names:

### 1. `tweenEasing` alias missing

Flash 8 JSFL uses `frame.tweenEasing` (the JsflFrame getter/setter at line 250) but `setFrameProperty` only handles `"ease"` (line 1062), not `"tweenEasing"`. JSFL scripts that call `tl.setFrameProperty("tweenEasing", 50)` silently fall through to the unhandled branch with no effect.

The JsflFrame proxy already exposes `tweenEasing` as a getter/setter (line 253), but `setFrameProperty` is the timeline-level batch API commonly used in JSFL authoring scripts and should support both names.

### 2. `soundLoop` / `soundLoops` not handled

Flash 8 JSFL uses `frame.soundLoop` to set the repeat count. The binary FLA format reads this as `soundLoop` (see `packages/core/src/fla/flash8-binary.ts:2562`), and the internal model stores it as `repeatCount`. The `setFrameProperty` implementation handles `"soundName"`, `"soundSync"`, and `"soundEffect"` but NOT `"soundLoop"` or `"soundLoops"`. 

JSFL scripts like `frame.setFrameProperty("soundLoop", 3)` to set looping have no effect.

## Fix

In `runtime.ts`, in the `setFrameProperty` switch/else-if chain (around line 1077), add:

```ts
} else if (property === "tweenEasing") {
  // Alias: Flash 8 JSFL uses "tweenEasing" as property name
  const easeVal = Math.max(-100, Math.min(100, Number(value)));
  mutateTimeline((tl) => ({
    ...tl,
    layers: tl.layers.map((l) => {
      if (l.id !== layerId) return l;
      return {
        ...l,
        frames: l.frames.map((f) => {
          if (!f.isKeyframe || f.index !== fi) return f;
          return { ...f, motionEase: easeVal };
        }),
      };
    }),
  }));
} else if (property === "soundLoop" || property === "soundLoops") {
  const loops = Math.max(0, Math.round(Number(value)));
  mutateTimeline((tl) => ({
    ...tl,
    layers: tl.layers.map((l) => {
      if (l.id !== layerId) return l;
      return {
        ...l,
        frames: l.frames.map((f) => {
          if (!f.isKeyframe || f.index !== fi) return f;
          if (!f.sound) return f;
          return { ...f, sound: { ...f.sound, repeatCount: loops } };
        }),
      };
    }),
  }));
}
```

## Files

- `packages/authoring-ui/src/jsfl/runtime.ts` — around line 1062 (inside `setFrameProperty`)
